---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
import Jobtitle from "../components/cv/Jobtitle.astro";
// import DownloadCV from '../components/cv/downloadcv.astro';
import DownloadCV from "../components/cv/DownloadResume";
import Skill from "../components/cv/Skill.astro";

---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/5.15.2/css/all.min.css">

<BaseLayout title="Resume">
  <!-- <div class="mb-3">
    <a href="/public/resume.pdf" download id="downloadButton">
      <span style="font-size: 1.2em; cursor: pointer;">⬇</span>
    </a>
  </div> -->

  <div>
    <div class="mb-6 text-center">
      <div class="text-4xl font-bold">Zaheer Ud Din</div>
      <div class="text-xl opacity-80 mt-1">Staff Consultant Engineer</div>
      <div class="text-sm opacity-70 mt-2">
        +92-311-5076756 &nbsp;|&nbsp; zaheeru7@gmail.com &nbsp;|&nbsp; Islamabad, Pakistan
      </div>
      <div class="text-sm mt-1">
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/zaheeru7" target="_blank" class="hover:underline">linkedin.com/in/zaheeru7</a>
        &nbsp;|&nbsp;
        <a href="https://github.com/zaheeruddeen" target="_blank" class="hover:underline">github.com/zaheeruddeen</a>
        &nbsp;|&nbsp;
        <a href="https://zaheeruddeen.github.io/portfolio" target="_blank" class="hover:underline">zaheeruddeen.github.io/portfolio</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-4" style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
      <div class="text-3xl font-bold">Professional Summary</div>
      <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZaheerUdDeen/portfolio/main/public/resume.pdf" download id="downloadButton">
        <i class="fas fa-download" style="font-size: 1.2em; cursor: pointer;"></i>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
      I'm the engineer teams bring in when the system that "works fine" starts cracking under real use.
      I'm also who they call when the monolith everyone's afraid to touch needs to become something the
      business can actually grow on. I've spent 8+ years doing exactly that. Most recently, I've been
      federating product-catalog and identity events across STC's OSS/BSS systems at DNext. Before that,
      I turned a manual billing process at BILL.com into a fully automated, zero-loss delivery system. I
      also led the platform revamp at Global Rescue that Fast Company recognized as one of the most
      innovative products of 2024. I lead small teams, ship production systems that other teams end up
      depending on, and make sure the engineers around me are shipping better too.
    </div>

    <div class="mb-5">
      <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Core Competencies</div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-10 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6">
      <div>
        <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold mb-1">Languages, Frameworks & Frontend</div>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-4">
          <Skill name="Java 8/17/21" link="https://www.oracle.com/java/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Spring Boot" link="https://spring.io/projects/spring-boot/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Micronaut" link="https://micronaut.io/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="React 19" link="https://react.dev/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Angular Micro-Frontends" link="https://angular.io/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
        </ul>

        <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold mb-1">Cloud, Containers & CI/CD</div>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-4">
          <Skill
            name="AWS"
            link="https://aws.amazon.com/"
            style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;"
            subSkills={[
              { name: "Lambda", link: "https://aws.amazon.com/lambda/" },
              { name: "ECS/Fargate", link: "https://aws.amazon.com/fargate/" },
              { name: "RDS", link: "https://aws.amazon.com/rds/" },
              { name: "S3", link: "https://aws.amazon.com/s3/" },
              { name: "KMS", link: "https://aws.amazon.com/kms/" },
            ]}
          />
          <Skill name="Docker" link="https://www.docker.com/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Kubernetes" link="https://kubernetes.io/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Jenkins" link="https://www.jenkins.io/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="CI/CD Automation" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
        </ul>

        <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold mb-1">Data & Messaging</div>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-6">
          <Skill name="Oracle" link="https://www.oracle.com/database/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="PostgreSQL" link="https://www.postgresql.org/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="MySQL" link="https://www.mysql.com/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="DynamoDB" link="https://aws.amazon.com/dynamodb/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Kafka" link="https://kafka.apache.org/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="RabbitMQ" link="https://www.rabbitmq.com/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="SQS/SNS" link="https://aws.amazon.com/sqs/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold mb-1">Architecture & Security</div>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-4">
          <Skill name="Event-Driven & Serverless Architecture" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="OAuth 2.0" link="https://oauth.net/2/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="OIDC/SAML" link="https://openid.net/connect/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Keycloak" link="https://www.keycloak.org/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
        </ul>

        <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold mb-1">Testing, Observability & Practices</div>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-6">
          <Skill name="JUnit 5" link="https://junit.org/junit5/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Mockito" link="https://site.mockito.org/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="TestContainers" link="https://testcontainers.com/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Datadog" link="https://www.datadoghq.com/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Splunk Cloud" link="https://www.splunk.com/" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
          <Skill name="Agile/Scrum, Kanban, Sprint Planning" style="color: #232F3E; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #232F3E;" />
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-5">
      <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Professional Experience</div>
    </div>

    <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
      <Jobtitle
        title="Staff Software Consultant"
        companyDescription="DNext — Client: STC (Saudi Telecommunications, BSS/OSS Federation)"
        companyName="DNext"
        style="color: #4a4e91; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #4a4e91;"
        fromDate="July/01/2026"
        toDate="Present"
      >
        <p class="text-sm italic mb-2">
          Tech: Java, Spring Boot, Apache Kafka, Avro (Confluent Schema Registry), Camunda 7 (BPMN),
          Keycloak, Angular, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Docker
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc columns-1 md:columns-2 mx-6">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            STC's BSS/OSS synchronization engine federates product-catalog changes from the master
            product catalogue out to downstream systems — CPQ (Configure, Price, Quote), ECOM
            (E-Commerce channel, via Ericsson Catalog Manager), and OCS (Online Charging System,
            Ericsson). Orchestrates the flow through Camunda BPMN workflows.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Ramping into the engine's event-processing pipeline: contributed to sequencing of
            event-group processing, and added Avro-schema Kafka topic integration for user onboarding
            and role-assignment events, extending the existing publish/listener flow to carry identity
            and access-lifecycle events through the same federation pipeline.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
      <Jobtitle
        title="Staff Consultant Engineer"
        companyDescription="10Pearls — Client: BILL.com (US Fintech, AP/AR Automation)"
        companyName="10Pearls"
        companyLink="https://www.10pearls.com/"
        style="color: #a15c2f; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #a15c2f;"
        fromDate="December/01/2025"
        toDate="July/01/2026"
      >
        <p class="text-sm italic mb-2">
          Tech: Java 17+, Micronaut 4, Kafka, Flink, AWS (ECS/Fargate, RDS, S3, SQS/SNS, KMS),
          Angular/React 19, Docker, Datadog, Splunk Cloud
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc columns-1 md:columns-2 mx-6">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Closed a gap where customers on BILL.com's Supplier Payments Plus were getting invoices but
            no email statements: designed and shipped an end-to-end notification pipeline using an
            async outbox + CDC + Kafka + Flink pattern, delivering automated PDF billing statements
            with zero-loss delivery and zero manual intervention.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Owned the pipeline end to end — recipient lookup, template assembly, PDF generation, secure
            S3 upload — and established the data boundary between the Billing Engine and Billing
            Facade, resolving a recurring source of cross-team integration friction.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
      <Jobtitle
        title="Senior Software Engineer & Team Lead"
        companyDescription="Global Rescue provides medical, security, intelligence, and crisis response services to corporations, governments and individuals"
        companyName="Global Rescue"
        companyLink="https://www.globalrescue.com/"
        style="color: #722F37; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #722F37;"
        fromDate="March/01/2022"
        toDate="November/01/2025"
      >
        <ul class="list-disc columns-1 md:columns-2 mx-6">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            When I joined, Global Rescue was running on an aging monolith that couldn't keep up with
            the business. Over 3.5 years, I spearheaded the GRID 2.0 revamp that broke it into
            microservices. Customer renewals jumped after the beta, and Fast Company put Global Rescue
            on its Most Innovative Companies list in 2024 — recognition specifically tied to the system
            we rebuilt.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Led a team of 6 engineers. My job wasn't just assigning tickets — it was setting
            architectural direction, running design reviews, mentoring mid-level engineers into senior
            roles, and being the bridge between US-based product leadership and our distributed
            engineering team.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            The company had three separate authentication flows that nobody fully understood. I
            consolidated them into a single identity layer — OAuth 2.0 + OIDC via Keycloak with custom
            SSO support, API Gateway integration, and backward compatibility through dynamic proxies.
            One system instead of three.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Built the internal platform libraries that other teams now depend on: an auth SDK, a
            circuit-breaker messaging layer, and a unified notification service for email, push, and
            SMS. It's the kind of quiet infrastructure that prevents outages and saves every team weeks
            of reinventing the wheel.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Created a custom monitoring system for the company's most critical API (SOS emergency
            calls). If that endpoint goes down, lives are at risk. My integration-testing framework
            with synthetic monitoring caught regressions before they ever hit production.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Defined the API contracts that let front-end teams (React and Angular) build in parallel
            with backend — cutting the integration phase from weeks to days.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
      <Jobtitle
        title="Software Engineer"
        companyName="Stella Technologies"
        companyDescription="Stella Technology, based in Silicon Valley, is a leading digital healthcare-only company."
        companyLink="https://stellatechnology.com/"
        style="color: #287c6e; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #287c6e;"
        fromDate="March/01/2021"
        toDate="March/01/2022"
      >
        <ul class="list-disc columns-1 md:columns-2 mx-6">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Stella had a healthcare platform that could talk to its own database but not to anyone
            else's. I engineered the HL7 & FHIR interoperability layer that opened it up to outside
            systems — unlocking data exchange partnerships that became a new revenue stream.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Replaced a fragile cron-based data pipeline with serverless ETL on AWS Lambda and Step
            Functions. Data latency dropped from hours to near real time, and the on-call team stopped
            getting paged for pipeline failures.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Introduced testing discipline where there was none: coverage gates, test-first culture, and
            a safety net that let us refactor aggressively without breaking things.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
      <Jobtitle
        title="Software Engineer"
        companyName="China Mobile Pakistan - Zong 4G"
        companyDescription="Zong is a subsidiary of China Mobile in Pakistan & a leading telecome company with largest share of subscriber based in Pakistan."
        companyLink="https://www.zong.com.pk/about-zong/china-mobile-pakistan/"
        style="color: #567d30; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #567d30;"
        fromDate="April/01/2020"
        toDate="March/01/2021"
      >
        <ul class="list-disc columns-1 md:columns-2 mx-6">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Took the AutoKiosk Machine from whiteboard to production for one of Pakistan's largest
            telecom providers. Owned planning, building, testing, and go-live.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Shipped features for MyZong (millions of subscribers) while navigating tight sprints and
            cross-cultural collaboration with Chinese vendor teams.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>

      <Jobtitle
        title="Software Engineer"
        companyName="Taj Digital Healthcare"
        companyDescription="TAJ is a digital healthcare service available instantly, smart & personalised with a user experience that appeals to everyone and distributed efficiently with great customer services"
        companyLink="https://www.tajdigitalhealth.com/"
        style="color: #2a8988; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #2a8988;"
        fromDate="July/01/2018"
        toDate="March/01/2020"
      >
        <ul class="list-disc columns-1 md:columns-2 mx-6">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Joined as a junior; left as the primary backend engineer. Built TAJ's digital healthcare
            platform from an MVP into a fully operational business within a year — the product that
            taught me what it means to own something end to end.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Designed a referral engine that went viral on launch day: 10,000+ downloads in the first
            release, becoming the product's main growth channel before any paid marketing.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Connected Total Care Saudi, insurance companies, pharmacies, and labs into a multi-tenant
            partner ecosystem for online medicine and lab ordering.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-5">
      <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
    </div>

    <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
      <TimeLineElement
        title="Bachelor of Software Engineering"
        subtitle="2014 to 2018 at Bahria University, Islamabad, Pakistan"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="mb-5">
      <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Awards, Entrepreneurship & Additional</div>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10">
      <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
        Winner, HEC Blockchain Hackathon 2018. 1st Place, Bahria University Open House 2018 (Engineering).
      </li>
      <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
        Founded Pharmaconn (healthcare startup, won YES Competition).
      </li>
      <li class="mb-1 text-justify">Co-founded Porter ($20K pre-seed).</li>
      <li class="mb-1 text-justify">English (Fluent), Urdu (Native).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
